<v LaDonna  Powell>Like, take your book. She would always say that, because in West India, they say, "take your book," meaning "go to school." She's like, you don't need bagga fren, you don't need man, you don't need-- you need your book. I'm like, OK, this lady.
<v LaDonna  Powell>比如，带上你的书。她总是这么说，因为在西印度，他们说“take your book”，意思是“去上学”。她说，你不需要朋友，你不需要男人，你不需要……你需要你的书。我说，好吧，这位女士。

00:35:33.220 --> 00:36:12.880
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>LaDonna was improvising her own book, her own workplace manifesto. She had gathered bits and pieces from this book and that one, adding her own experience, her insights, wisdom from her mom. And she was trying it out on her first audience. For a long time, LaDonna had imagined what her book would be if she ever wrote one. She told me she had even thought of a title, Do a Little More-- it's something her mom used to say to her. And her trainings did what all those best-selling motivational books do. She said, do what I did, it can work for you too. She encouraged them to push themselves, imagine themselves on a grand stage.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>LaDonna在即兴创作她自己的书，她自己的工作场所宣言。她从这本书和那本书里收集片段，加入自己的经验、洞察力，以及妈妈的智慧。她正在第一批听众身上试验。很长一段时间以来，LaDonna一直想象如果她写书会写什么。她告诉我，她甚至想好了一个标题，“多做一点”——这是她妈妈过去常对她说的话。她的培训产生了那些畅销励志书所能产生的所有效果。她说，做我做的，这对你也有用。她鼓励他们逼自己一把，想象自己身处宏大的舞台。

00:36:12.880 --> 00:36:22.810
<v LaDonna Powell>Don't be afraid. Be motivated to go forward. You do a little more than the other workers and do your training, you elevate. You're worth it. It was like, you're definitely worth it.
<v LaDonna Powell>不要害怕。要有前进的动力。你比其他员工多做一点，完成培训，你就会提升。你值得这样做。就像，你绝对值得。

00:36:22.810 --> 00:36:45.440
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>People were into it. I talked to guards who went through the LaDonna Powell training, and it was a thing. It was motivating and clear. LaDonna trained hundreds of people after that-- new recruits, and she started to do refresher trainings for the existing guards. People would leave class saying, we're going to vote Powell for president. You've got my vote, Powell.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>人们很投入。我和参加过LaDonna Powell培训的保安谈过，这确实是一回事。它充满动力且清晰。此后LaDonna培训了数百人——新入职的人，她还开始为现有保安进行复训。人们离开教室时会说，我们要投Powell当总统。你得到我的选票了，Powell。

00:36:45.440 --> 00:36:59.340
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She taught people from retail jobs and former military people, men and women. She liked them. The women were focused-- not on sexual favors but on work. There was one in her class who was super talkative, opinionated.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她培训了来自零售行业的人和前军人，男女都有。她喜欢他们。女性很专注——不是为了性恩惠，而是为了工作。她的班上有个人超级健谈，有自己的主见。

