00:43:15.200 --> 00:43:33.080
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>The woman did not want to be interviewed for the radio. She wanted to handle this her own way. LaDonna wanted to go to upper management, but the woman didn't want to. She wanted to keep her job. She told LaDonna she didn't need anything to be done. To LaDonna, that was acceptance.
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>那个女人不想接受广播采访。她想用自己的方式处理。LaDonna想找高层管理人员，但那个女人不想。她想保住工作。她告诉LaDonna她不需要做任何事。对LaDonna来说，那是接受。

00:43:33.080 --> 00:43:52.180
<v LaDonna Powell>People are not supposed to take from you without your permission. I just wanted her to understand she's worth fighting for. They should make you feel worth fighting for. She just-- ugh, she just doesn't see it that way.
<v LaDonna Powell>人们不应该在没有你允许的情况下从你那里索取。我只是想让她明白她值得抗争。他们应该让你觉得你值得抗争。她只是……呃，她就是看不开。

00:43:52.180 --> 00:44:27.480
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>And there was nothing, no evidence LaDonna could point to to convince her otherwise. LaDonna was trying to force a reckoning that would require this woman, and everyone on staff, to see themselves differently, to be vigilant at all times. But many of them were flagging. They were losing their sense of urgency, turning inward, away from revolution. LaDonna never turned away. Nine months after this, she was pulled into a meeting with HR and the project manager, the big boss at Allied JFK.
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>没有任何证据能让LaDonna说服她。LaDonna试图强迫一种清算，这要求这个女人和所有员工以不同的方式看待自己，时刻保持警惕。但他们中的许多人都在动摇。他们正在失去紧迫感，转向内部，远离革命。LaDonna从未转向。九个月后，她被叫去与人力资源部门和项目经理，即Allied肯尼迪机场的大老板开会。

00:44:27.480 --> 00:44:36.950
<v LaDonna Powell>I was like, am I fired? I asked three times. Am I fired? Tell me what I'm fired for. Am I fired for talking up?
<v LaDonna Powell>我说，我被开除了吗？我问了三次。我被开除了吗？告诉我我为什么被开除。我是因为说话被开除的吗？

00:44:36.950 --> 00:44:47.240
<v LaDonna Powell>And he's like, oh, I wish you would close your mouth. And I said, what am I fired for? And I started reeling off everything. Am I fired for talking up? About what, the sexual harassment? About being called a nigger?
<v LaDonna Powell>他说，哦，我希望你能闭上嘴。我说，我为什么被开除？我开始列举一切。我是因为说话被开除的吗？关于什么，性骚扰？关于被叫黑鬼？

00:44:47.240 --> 00:45:01.080
<v LaDonna Powell>And I started saying ev-- I said, all the stuff that goes on in this place, everybody sleeping with everybody, people don't even do their job. And I just started saying everything to him. I said, so am I fired? No, you're not fired. We'll call you in a few days, and we'll let you know something.
<v LaDonna Powell>我开始说所……我说，这地方发生的所有事，每个人都和每个人睡觉，人们甚至不好好工作。我开始对他说了所有事。我说，那我被开除了吗？不，你没被开除。我们几天后会叫你，我们会通知你一些事。

00:45:01.080 --> 00:45:27.310
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>LaDonna says they didn't call. Weeks later, when she logged into Allied's online portal, that's where she saw she had been terminated. LaDonna had cycled through so many different strategies at Allied, but she had actually never thought about a lawsuit until this point. And when she talked to a lawyer, the lawyer said, this would be a stronger case if you knew other people had experienced the same thing.
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>LaDonna说他们没打电话。几周后，当她登录Allied的在线门户网站时，看到自己已被终止合同。LaDonna在Allied尝试过这么多不同的策略，但在此之前她从未想过诉讼。当她和律师交谈时，律师说，如果你知道其他人也有同样的经历，这个案子会更有力。

00:45:27.310 --> 00:45:39.310
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>I do, LaDonna said. I trained them. I trained everybody. I was a supervisor. I saw everything. The lawyer perked up. Well, if you can get other people to join you, you'd have a stronger case.
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>我知道，LaDonna说。我培训过他们。我培训了所有人。我是主管。我看到了一切。律师振作了起来。好吧，如果你能让其他人加入你，你的案子会更有力。

00:45:39.310 --> 00:46:10.530
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>LaDonna sat down, made a list of women she knew had experienced harassment and were no longer at Allied, and one morning she went through the list. The first woman she called said, I can't talk. She wouldn't explain why. LaDonna called the second woman, can't talk. Again, why? Eventually, this woman explained she had already sued Allied herself, settled the case, and signed a non-disclosure agreement-- an NDA. Next woman LaDonna called, same thing.
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>LaDonna坐下来，列了一份她知道经历过骚扰且已不在Allied工作的女性名单，一天早上她把名单过了一遍。她打的第一个女人说，我不能说。她不解释为什么。LaDonna给第二个女人打电话，不能说。再次，为什么？最终，这个女人解释说她自己已经起诉了Allied，达成了和解，并签署了一份保密协议——NDA。LaDonna打给下一个女人，也是一样。

00:46:10.530 --> 00:46:17.680
<v LaDonna  Powell>Wow. This is what they've been doing. These guys are still here. It's insane. It's kind of insane to me.
<v LaDonna  Powell>哇。这就是他们一直在做的事。这些家伙还在那。这太疯狂了。对我来说有点疯狂。

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:20.770
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>Did you even know that was an option?
<v Chana  Joffe-Walt>你甚至知道那是一个选项吗？

00:46:20.770 --> 00:46:21.690
<v LaDonna Powell>I didn't.
<v LaDonna Powell>我不知道。

00:46:21.690 --> 00:46:22.570
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊。

00:46:22.570 --> 00:46:28.790
<v LaDonna Powell>But you know what? It's not an option. I hope you guys are listening. It's not an option.
<v LaDonna Powell>但你知道吗？这不是一个选项。我希望你们在听。这不是一个选项。

00:46:28.790 --> 00:46:32.110
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Wait, who are you talking to, "I hope you guys are listening"?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>等等，你在和谁说话，“我希望你们在听”？

00:46:32.110 --> 00:46:32.790
<v LaDonna Powell>Allied.
<v LaDonna Powell>Allied。

00:46:32.790 --> 00:46:33.500
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oh.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哦。

00:46:33.500 --> 00:46:43.230
<v LaDonna Powell>I hope they're listening because I feel like, how many times do they get to do that? How many times do they get to do that before they actually take this serious and start making a change?
<v LaDonna Powell>我希望他们在听，因为我觉得，他们能做多少次这种事？在他们真正认真对待并开始做出改变之前，他们能做多少次？

00:46:43.230 --> 00:47:16.760
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>We found court records for 11 lawsuits against Allied at JFK that allege workplace discrimination. It's unclear how many more Allied might have settled before the cases formally went to court. So LaDonna wasn't alone trying to push back. Other women were fighting back too. She had no idea. They did come forward. The information was conveyed to a higher authority, to a court of law, and it did not make LaDonna or these women more secure. It made them invisible.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我们找到了11起针对Allied在肯尼迪机场工作歧视的诉讼法庭记录。不清楚Allied在案件正式上庭前可能和解了多少起。所以LaDonna并不是唯一一个试图反抗的人。其他女性也在反抗。她根本不知道。她们确实站了出来。信息被传达给了更高的权威，传达给了法庭，但这并没有让LaDonna或这些女性更安全。它让她们隐形了。

00:47:16.760 --> 00:47:37.060
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>LaDonna filed her lawsuit last October. Soon after, three more people from Allied got in touch, asking to join her lawsuit. And then, after that, there were two more workplace discrimination lawsuits filed against Allied at other New York sites-- the World Trade Center and LaGuardia Airport. LaDonna waited. Everyone has a boss.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>LaDonna去年十月提起了诉讼。不久之后，另外三个来自Allied的人联系了她，要求加入她的诉讼。此后，在Allied其他纽约站点——世界贸易中心和拉瓜迪亚机场——又提起了两起工作歧视诉讼。LaDonna等待着。每个人都有老板。

00:47:37.060 --> 00:47:46.010
<v LaDonna Powell>What else do you guys need to happen-- just what else, before you say, all right, let's get these guys out of here, they've went too far?
<v LaDonna Powell>你们还需要发生什么——到底还需要什么，你们才会说，好了，把这些人赶走，他们做得太过分了？

00:47:46.010 --> 00:47:52.000
<v Steve Jones>OK, my name is Steve Jones, and I'm the CEO of Allied Universal.
<v Steve Jones>好的，我的名字是Steve Jones，我是Allied Universal的CEO。

00:47:52.000 --> 00:48:28.430
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Steve Jones became CEO in 2016 when his security company, Universal Services of America, merged with AlliedBarton, becoming the largest security firm in North America. He told me LaDonna was fired because of her failure to comply with her supervisory duties. He wouldn't say more about what duties but was clear it was not for speaking up about sexual harassment and racial discrimination. He said he only heard those complaints after LaDonna filed her lawsuit and there was a local news story about it. He adds, "This is despite Allied's many systems in place for employees to communicate concerns."
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Steve Jones在2016年成为CEO，当时他的安保公司Universal Services of America与AlliedBarton合并，成为北美最大的安保公司。他告诉我，LaDonna被开除是因为她未能履行主管职责。他没有具体说是什么职责，但很清楚不是因为举报性骚扰和种族歧视。他说他只有在LaDonna提起诉讼并且有当地新闻报道后才听到这些投诉。他补充说，“尽管Allied有许多供员工沟通顾虑的系统。”

00:48:28.430 --> 00:48:44.170
<v Steve Jones>There's literally a half a dozen avenues to where you could communicate to us, and then we would launch an immediate investigation. Why didn't LaDonna Powell choose to take one of those avenues of communication and inform us of it? I don't know. We're obviously--
<v Steve Jones>我们字面上有一半打通了你可以与我们沟通的渠道，然后我们会立即启动调查。为什么LaDonna Powell不选择其中一种沟通渠道通知我们？我不知道。我们显然……

00:48:44.170 --> 00:48:53.450
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So wait, you're saying she didn't-- you're saying that she did not report any of this behavior, verbally or in a written form to supervisors or HR?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>等等，你是说她没有……你是说她没有口头或书面形式向主管或人力资源部门报告任何这些行为吗？

00:48:53.450 --> 00:48:59.560
<v Steve Jones>What I'm telling you, yeah, is the first time we were made aware of this was through the media.
<v Steve Jones>我告诉你的是，是的，我们第一次通过媒体了解到这一点。

00:48:59.560 --> 00:49:41.370
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>There's lawsuits-- I mean, there's lawsuits going back to 2014. There's three lawsuits that describe very similar behavior that LaDonna is describing in the-- there's two more in 2015. There's formal complaints that I've seen written to HR that describe very similar behavior. There's calls to OSHA about being denied bathroom breaks. There's an employee at Allied JFK who left a letter and distributed it publicly that described widespread sexual misconduct by supervisors. And not to mention, I've been talking to many, many staff at Allied who have heard about these things. So it does not seem true that you were not made aware of some of the issues that LaDonna's raising.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>有诉讼……我的意思是，诉讼可以追溯到2014年。有三起诉讼描述了LaDonna在……中描述的非常相似的行为，2015年还有两起。我见过写给人力资源的正式投诉，描述了非常相似的行为。有人给OSHA打电话投诉被拒绝上厕所。Allied肯尼迪机场的一名员工留了一封信并公开发布，描述了主管们广泛的性不当行为。更不用说，我一直在和Allied的许多员工交谈，他们都听说过这些事。所以你并不知晓LaDonna提出的问题，这似乎不是真的。

00:49:41.370 --> 00:50:01.440
<v Steve Jones>So what I would tell you is LaDonna Powell did not make us aware of her specific claims. And what I would say is, with regards to any other claims, every claim that gets brought to our attention is investigated thoroughly and responded to. And obviously, if it's a pending legal matter, I clearly can't comment on that.
<v Steve Jones>所以我可以告诉你的是，LaDonna Powell没有让我们知晓她的具体主张。我想说的是，关于任何其他主张，每一个引起我们注意的主张都会经过彻底调查并做出回应。显然，如果这是一个未决的法律事项，我显然无法评论。

00:50:01.440 --> 00:50:12.040
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>No, they were settled. There are lawsuits that were settled. And for the most part, it seems like the people who settled those lawsuits signed nondisclosure agreements, so they can't talk about it.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>不，它们已经和解了。有些诉讼已经和解了。而且大多数情况下，似乎那些和解诉讼的人签署了保密协议，所以他们不能谈论它。

00:50:12.040 --> 00:50:24.230
<v Steve Jones>OK. That does not change the fact that we don't take all allegations of either harassment or discrimination very, very seriously, and then we investigate each and every one of them.
<v Steve Jones>好的。这并不能改变我们没有非常、非常认真地对待所有骚扰或歧视指控的事实，我们会对每一项进行调查。

00:50:24.230 --> 00:50:51.050
<v Chana   Joffe-Walt>One of the things that did not make sense to me was, if there are multiple complaints about certain employees, and Allied is having to pay out money in settlements over and over, why not just get rid of those managers? Setting aside what's fair or what's right, it just seems like there'd be strong financial reasons to do that. I asked him what he made of the fact that some of the same men were accused again and again.
<v Chana   Joffe-Walt>对我来说不合理的一件事是，如果有关于某些员工的多项投诉，而且Allied不得不一次又一次地支付和解金，为什么不直接摆脱那些经理？撇开公平或正确不谈，似乎财务上有充分的理由这样做。我问他，有些人反复被指控，他对此怎么看。

00:50:51.050 --> 00:51:03.530
<v Steve Jones>We can't speculate that because someone has an allegation that that means those facts are correct. Again, our position--
<v Steve Jones>我们不能因为有人提出了指控就推测事实是正确的。再次声明，我们的立场……

00:51:03.530 --> 00:51:15.070
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Of course, but it's repeated. I mean, that's the difference, right? It's not a single allegation. It's repeated allegations that are similar to one another against the same people.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当然，但它是重复的。我的意思是，那是区别，对吧？不是单一的指控。是针对同一批人反复出现相似的指控。

00:51:15.070 --> 00:51:35.550
<v Steve Jones>And again, any time an allegation is made, we conduct a thorough investigation-- is that allegation true? Is there a portion of it that is true? And what type of behavior was being done or wasn't being done? We have to get to the facts.
<v Steve Jones>再次声明，任何时候有人提出指控，我们都会进行彻底调查——那个指控是真的吗？它是部分真实吗？做了什么行为或没做什么？我们必须弄清事实。

00:51:35.550 --> 00:52:09.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Allied says that is what they're trying to do now. They told me that since the lawsuit was filed, JFK management and supervisors have received training on discrimination and harassment, and HR staff got specialized training on how to respond to such matters. They've launched their own investigation and an independent investigation into what happened. Those investigations got started seven months ago-- which, to be clear, was four years after LaDonna says she first complained verbally and filed a written complaint against Kevin.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Allied说这就是他们现在正努力做的。他们告诉我，自从诉讼提起以来，肯尼迪机场的管理层和主管接受了关于歧视和骚扰的培训，人力资源人员接受了如何处理此类事项的专业培训。他们已经启动了自己内部的调查，以及对所发生事件的独立调查。那些调查在七个月前就开始了——这需要明确一下，是在LaDonna说她第一次口头抱怨并对Kevin提起书面投诉四年后。

00:52:09.460 --> 00:52:44.030
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Kevin and the four other men named in LaDonna's lawsuit denied all the allegations to us through their lawyers. I got an email response from the lawyer for Kevin McNamara and Chris Timberlake and the head boss at Allied JFK, Martin Feeney. It said, "We're confident that once the facts of the case come to light, it will be clear that Mr. Feeney, Mr. Timberlake, and Mr. McNamara did nothing wrong. It is unfortunate that these individuals' professional reputations are being tarnished as this case is debated in the court of public opinion."
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Kevin和LaDonna诉讼中提到的其他四个人通过律师向我们否认了所有指控。我收到了Kevin McNamara、Chris Timberlake和Allied肯尼迪机场老板Martin Feeney的律师的电子邮件回复。上面写着，“我们相信一旦案件事实大白，就会清楚Feeney先生、Timberlake先生和McNamara先生没有做错任何事。不幸的是，当这个案件在公众舆论的法庭上争论不休时，这些人的专业声誉正受到玷污。”

00:52:44.030 --> 00:53:14.000
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>There is one other investigation to come out of this lawsuit. The Port Authority, which runs New York's airports, says it is now reviewing LaDonna's allegations, and others, as well. A statement from the Port Authority says, they'll "take aggressive measures against Allied if they find those allegations to be true." And then, just recently, I started to hear rumors about some aggressive measures. I started to hear that the entire leadership of Allied JFK was gone.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>此诉讼还有另一项调查。负责纽约机场的港务局表示，它现在也在审查LaDonna的指控以及其他指控。港务局的一份声明称，如果发现那些指控属实，他们将“对Allied采取积极措施”。然后，就在最近，我开始听到一些关于积极措施的传闻。我开始听说Allied肯尼迪机场的整个领导层都走了。

00:53:14.000 --> 00:53:15.930
<v Female Guard  1>Oh, it's beautiful now.
<v Female Guard  1>哦，现在好多了。

00:53:15.930 --> 00:53:22.530
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This is a guard who works at Allied currently. She didn't want me to use her name. None of these workers did.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这是一名目前在Allied工作的保安。她不想让我使用她的名字。这些工人都不想。

00:53:22.530 --> 00:53:31.670
<v Female Guard 2>I didn't believe it at first, because I thought maybe it was just a rumor, but then my phone started blowing up, so I was like, oh, wow. Wow.
<v Female Guard 2>起初我不敢相信，因为我以为那只是谣言，但后来我的手机炸了，所以我想，哦，哇。哇。

00:53:31.670 --> 00:53:41.470
<v Male Guard>Yeah, it's about time. It's like, how can they get away with this, and why isn't someone doing something about it?
<v Male Guard>是啊，是时候了。就像，他们怎么能逃脱惩罚，为什么没有人对此做点什么？

00:53:41.470 --> 00:53:52.310
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The Allied guards say management did not explain what happened to the supervisors, or even why something was done. But they say they all know why it was done-- LaDonna.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Allied保安说，管理层没有解释主管们发生了什么，甚至没有解释为什么要采取某种行动。但他们说他们都知道原因——LaDonna。

00:53:52.310 --> 00:54:03.340
<v Female Guard 1>I love it. I thank her for moving all these no-good people out, who have so many records on accusing women and doing all that stuff. I thank her.
<v Female Guard 1>我喜欢。我感谢她把所有这些没用的、有那么多指控女性记录和做所有那些事的人赶走。我感谢她。

00:54:03.340 --> 00:54:11.760
<v Male Guard>And for years, you've heard the people doing stuff. And all of a sudden, bingo, finally something was getting taken care of. Yeah.
<v Male Guard>多年来，你听到了人们在做那些事。然后突然，宾果，终于有事被处理了。是啊。

00:54:11.760 --> 00:54:24.490
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>A lot of people I spoke with didn't want to share their opinions on the record at all. And then there was this woman, who said she couldn't talk to me, but then stood next to her coworker yelling while I interviewed him.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我和许多人交谈，他们根本不想公开分享自己的观点。然后是这个女人，她说她不能跟我说话，但在我采访她同事时站在旁边大喊大叫。

00:54:24.490 --> 00:54:28.010
<v Male Guard>Yeah. They said that women are tired of what's going on--
<v Male Guard>是啊。她们说女性对发生的事感到厌倦——

00:54:28.010 --> 00:54:29.490
<v Female Guard 3>Yeah, you get tired of it.
<v Female Guard 3>是啊，你厌倦了。

00:54:29.490 --> 00:54:30.840
<v Male Guard>It's true. It's like, you know--
<v Male Guard>这是真的。就像，你知道……

00:54:30.840 --> 00:54:33.260
<v Female Guard 3>After a while, [INAUDIBLE].
<v Female Guard 3>过了一会儿，[听不清]。

00:54:33.260 --> 00:54:35.370
<v Male Guard>Yeah, enough is enough. And--
<v Male Guard>是啊，够了就是够了。而且……

00:54:35.370 --> 00:54:38.200
<v Female Guard 3>It's always been a big issue.
<v Female Guard 3>这一直是个大问题。

00:54:38.200 --> 00:54:43.340
<v Male Guard>Yeah. As you said, it's always been a big issue.
<v Male Guard>是啊。就像你说的，这一直是个大问题。

00:54:43.340 --> 00:54:46.480
<v Female Guard  3>Women are speaking out now.
<v Female Guard  3>女性现在在发声。

00:54:46.480 --> 00:54:47.220
<v Male Guard>Yeah. Yeah.
<v Male Guard>是啊。是啊。

00:54:47.220 --> 00:55:04.000
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Allied told me three people were fired. They wouldn't tell me who. As far as I can tell, Kevin McNamara and Chris Timberlake were not fired. They, along with most of the leadership from Allied JFK, were reassigned-- meaning they still work for Allied but not at JFK. I asked Allied CEO Steve Jones why many of the supervisors were reassigned.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Allied告诉我三个人被开除了。他们没告诉我谁。据我所知，Kevin McNamara和Chris Timberlake没有被开除。他们和Allied肯尼迪机场的大多数领导层一起被重新分配了——这意味着他们仍然为Allied工作，但不在肯尼迪机场。我问Allied CEO Steve Jones，为什么许多主管被重新分配。

00:55:04.000 --> 00:55:11.880
<v Steve Jones>So, we reassign employees all the time, whether it's promotion opportunities or new different challenges or--
<v Steve Jones>所以，我们一直在重新分配员工，无论是晋升机会还是新的不同挑战还是……

00:55:11.880 --> 00:55:19.960
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Right. But are they being moved because they were at fault of some form of harassment or discrimination?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>对。但他们是因为犯了某种形式的骚扰或歧视才被调动的吗？

00:55:19.960 --> 00:55:24.830
<v Steve Jones>No. So, I would say-- are some of the allegations found to be true? I would say no.
<v Steve Jones>不。所以，我想说……指控中有属实的吗？我会说没有。

00:55:24.830 --> 00:55:28.660
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So why are people being reassigned?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那为什么人们被重新分配？

00:55:28.660 --> 00:55:34.790
<v Steve Jones>Well, again, we reassign people-- we reassign people all the time.
<v Steve Jones>嗯，再说一次，我们重新分配人员——我们一直在重新分配人员。

00:55:34.790 --> 00:55:49.640
<v LaDonna Powell>It's just not an answer. Somebody just say it. We hired these guys. They're animals. We fucked up. We must stop. As a company, we frown upon this, and we're making changes. What's so hard to say that?
<v LaDonna Powell>这根本不是答案。有人说出来就好了。我们雇佣了这些家伙。他们是野兽。我们搞砸了。我们必须停止。作为一家公司，我们不赞成这样做，我们正在做出改变。说出这些话有什么难的？

00:55:49.640 --> 00:56:16.640
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It occurred to me at some point that I've asked LaDonna the same question almost every time I've talked with her, did that make you feel powerful? I've asked her this about so many different things. Did that make you feel powerful when you made it to supervisor, when you were training all those people, when a fancy Manhattan law firm filed a lawsuit on your behalf, when the CEO of the company was responding directly to your complaints?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我曾有段时间想到，每次和她谈话时，我几乎都会问LaDonna同样的问题，这让你感到强大吗？关于那么多不同的事，我都这样问过她。当你升为主管时，当你培训所有那些人时，当一家高档曼哈顿律师事务所代表你提起诉讼时，当公司CEO直接回应你的投诉时，这让你感到强大吗？

00:56:16.640 --> 00:56:43.080
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>No. LaDonna's answer was always no. It did not make her feel powerful. It was the same when the leadership of Allied JFK was removed. LaDonna heard that news, especially the part about the men from Allied being reassigned, and she was not thinking about her power. She was thinking about theirs. She was imagining Kevin arriving at his new job, putting on his same Allied uniform every day.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>没有。LaDonna的回答总是没有。这没让她感到强大。Allied肯尼迪机场的领导层被免职时也是一样。LaDonna听到那个消息，特别是关于Allied的人被重新分配的部分，她想的不是自己的权力。她想的是他们的。她想象Kevin到达他的新工作地点，每天穿上同样的Allied制服。

00:56:43.080 --> 00:56:56.400
<v LaDonna Powell>That you can continue to walk around, just doing whatever you want to whomever you want, however, and nobody can touch you, it's almost like you're the boogeyman. You're untouchable.
<v LaDonna Powell>你仍然可以四处走动，对任何人做你想做的任何事，无论如何，没人能动你，这几乎就像你是怪物一样。你是不可触碰的。

00:56:56.400 --> 00:57:20.870
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What LaDonna could now see was that he was protected, thoroughly, and she was not. She was alone. What LaDonna believed from all those self-help books is you have the power. There may be barriers, but if you act right, set your mind right, if you're strategic and ingenious, you can thwart their efforts to take your power away.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>LaDonna现在能看到的是，他受到了保护，非常彻底，而她没有。她孤身一人。LaDonna从所有那些励志书中相信的是，你有力量。可能存在障碍，但如果你表现得体，心态端正，如果你有战略性且聪明，你可以阻挠他们夺走你的权力。

00:57:20.870 --> 00:58:00.250
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This news made her feel like, not really, because, yeah, everybody has a boss, but it was not just Kevin. It was not just the supervisors. It was also the project manager and the HR manager and the legal department at Allied Universal that paid women and the law that allows them to do that. It was a system designed to withstand her refusal to comply, to absorb her whole onslaught, all her strategic thought, passionately executed, carefully taught. It just ate it up and kept doing its thing. And now that LaDonna has seen all of that, she's not sure how to see herself.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这个消息让她觉得，不完全是，因为，是的，每个人都有老板，但不仅仅是Kevin。不仅仅是主管。还有Allied Universal的项目经理、人力资源经理、法律部门，他们支付钱给女性，还有法律允许他们那样做。这是一个设计用来抵御她拒绝配合的系统，用来吸收她所有的猛攻，所有她热情执行、仔细教授的战略思想。它只是把它吞了下去，继续做它的事。现在LaDonna看到了这一切，她不确定该如何看待自己。

00:58:00.250 --> 00:58:11.340
<v LaDonna Powell>I just-- I keep having these moments, like, it still leaves this lasting feeling that I was so vulnerable to these people, and they damaged me.
<v LaDonna Powell>我只是……我一直有这种时刻，就像，它仍然留下了这种持久的感觉，即我在这些人面前是如此脆弱，他们伤害了我。

00:58:11.340 --> 00:58:38.160
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That damage is not visible, except to her. LaDonna still works at the airport. She works for the government now, for Customs and Border Protection. She's making more money, and it's a more prestigious job. LaDonna walks Terminal Four, her torso doubled in size by her bulletproof vest, head high, scanning the area like someone who owns the place. A couple months back, she was at work--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那种伤害是看不见的，除了她自己。LaDonna仍然在机场工作。她现在为政府工作，为海关和边境保护局工作。她挣得更多，这是一份更有声望的工作。LaDonna走在四号航站楼，身体被防弹背心撑大了两倍，昂着头，扫描着该区域，就像这里的主人一样。几个月前，她在工作——

00:58:38.160 --> 00:58:48.220
<v LaDonna  Powell>And I'm walking. I have a M4 in my hand, my vest, pistol on my side. I'm walking, and I'm doing an escort. It's, like, five of us, and we're escorting someone. He's a diplomat.
<v LaDonna  Powell>我走着。手里拿着一把M4，背心，腰间有手枪。我走着，正在护送。就像，我们五个人，正在护送某人。他是外交官。

00:58:48.220 --> 00:58:50.710
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She's not allowed to say from where.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>不允许说来自哪里。

00:58:50.710 --> 00:59:03.080
<v LaDonna Powell>He gave us a little pin and everything from his country. It's a regular day. And so we're escorting him. And we're walking, and everything's fine. And then I see one of the men.
<v LaDonna Powell>他给了我们一点胸针和他国家的什么东西。这是正常的一天。所以我们护送他。走着，一切都很好。然后我看到了其中一个男人。

00:59:03.080 --> 00:59:16.880
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>One of the men from Allied, a supervisor named Osvaldo Ortiz, the guy LaDonna says let the guard bleed on herself instead of giving her a bathroom break. He was coming into Terminal Four to get a coffee from Dunkin' Donuts.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Allied的其中一个男人，一个叫Osvaldo Ortiz的主管，LaDonna说他让保安尿在身上而不让他上厕所的那个家伙。他正走进四号航站楼，从Dunkin' Donuts买咖啡。

00:59:16.880 --> 00:59:26.750
<v LaDonna Powell>And then I just-- literally, I'm walking, and I'm fine. I'm talking, duh-duh, we're laughing, very militant, walking. And I'm fine. I got my gun. I'm holding it like this.
<v LaDonna Powell>然后我只是……字面上，我走着，我很好。我说，嗒嗒，我们笑着，非常军事化地走着。我很好。我有枪。我像这样拿着它。

00:59:26.750 --> 00:59:35.480
<v LaDonna Powell>And I turn, and I get a sign of him. And then he sees me. And then I just turned my whole body, shifted to the left, and I ducked down.
<v LaDonna Powell>然后我转过身，看到了他。他看到了我。然后我转过整个身体，向左转，蹲了下去。

00:59:35.480 --> 00:59:48.000
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>LaDonna ducked as she was telling this to me. This is a man who, at this point in time, has no official power over her. She doesn't work for him. She's not financially dependent on him.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>LaDonna在告诉我这些时蹲下了。这是一个在此刻对她没有任何官方权力的人。她不为他工作。她不需要经济依赖他。

00:59:48.000 --> 01:00:05.210
<v LaDonna Powell>Literally, I am-- I felt afraid. It's like, I'm nervous. Like, I started sweating and everything. It's like, why am I scared of this guy? It doesn't make sense to me. Regardless of me being, oh, badass Customs Agent with a gun, still the sight of him makes me cringe.
<v LaDonna Powell>字面上，我——我感到害怕。就像，我很紧张。我开始出汗等等。就像，我为什么怕这个家伙？这对我来说说不通。不管我是个带着枪的坏蛋海关探员，仅仅看到他还是让我畏缩。

01:00:05.210 --> 01:00:08.540
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And you're escorting a fancy diplomat.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你还在护送一位高档外交官。

01:00:08.540 --> 01:00:09.400
<v LaDonna Powell>Exactly.
<v LaDonna Powell>准确地说。

01:00:09.400 --> 01:00:11.500
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Who's here for important business.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>他来这里办重要业务的。

01:00:11.500 --> 01:00:12.260
<v LaDonna Powell>Yes.
<v LaDonna Powell>是的。

01:00:12.260 --> 01:00:15.790
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Who needs your protection because you are able to provide protection.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>他需要你的保护，因为你有能力提供保护。

01:00:15.790 --> 01:00:19.870
<v LaDonna Powell>Protection. Right, right. And then I feel like I couldn't protect myself in that moment, yes.
<v LaDonna Powell>保护。对，对。然后我觉得在那一刻我无法保护自己，是的。

01:00:19.870 --> 01:00:21.800
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And you have a gun.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>而且你有枪。

01:00:21.800 --> 01:00:24.820
<v LaDonna Powell>And I have a gun. It's kind of horrible.
<v LaDonna Powell>而且我有枪。这有点可怕。

01:00:24.820 --> 01:00:26.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah. And that guy has a Dunkin' Donuts coffee.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊。而那个家伙拿着Dunkin' Donuts的咖啡。

01:00:26.890 --> 01:00:36.790
<v LaDonna Powell>Coffee And I still feel, yeah, at his mercy. So power? No. I feel like I am caged because of them.
<v LaDonna Powell>咖啡。我仍然觉得，是的，任他摆布。所以权力？没有。我觉得我因为他们被囚禁了。

01:00:36.790 --> 01:01:07.550
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The cage is invisible, of course-- or it was until recently, just like the NDAs, and the reassignments, and everything else LaDonna can now see. She's still trying to map the contours of this cage, its full size and shape. It's hard. It's not written down anywhere or clearly marked. And that's what makes it scary. LaDonna needs to know exactly what she's dealing with. Then she can figure out her next move.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>囚笼当然是隐形的——或者直到最近，就像保密协议、重新分配，以及LaDonna现在能看到的其他一切。她仍然在试图绘制这个囚笼的轮廓、它的大小和形状。很难。它没写在任何地方，也没清晰标注。这就是它可怕的地方。LaDonna需要确切知道她在处理什么。然后她可以弄清楚她的下一步动作。

01:01:07.550 --> 01:01:20.050
<v Ira       Glass>Chana Joffe-Walt is one of the producers of our program.
<v Ira       Glass>Chana Joffe-Walt是我们节目的制作人之一。

01:01:20.050 --> 01:01:34.470
<v Ira       Glass>[MUSIC PLAYING - "SECURITY" BY ETTA JAMES]
<v Ira       Glass>[音乐播放 - Etta James的“Security”]

01:01:34.470 --> 01:02:00.720
<v Ira Glass>Well, our program was produced today by Diane Wu. The people who put together a show includes Zoe Chace, Dana Chivvis, Sean Cole, Chana Joffe-Walt, Seth Lind, Miki Meek, Alvin Melathe, Nadia Reiman, Robyn Semien, Christopher Swetala, and Matt Tierney. Our senior producer is Brian Reed. Our managing editor is Susan Burton. Mixing help today from Katherine Rae Mondo and Sharif Youssef. Editing help from Sarah Koenig and Nancy Updike. Special thanks today Rebecca [? Vitale-Dokolah, ?] Nava EtShalom, [? Amina ?] [? Kotkin, ?] and Matt Chase.
<v Ira Glass>好吧，我们的节目今天由Diane Wu制作。把节目放在一起的人包括Zoe Chace、Dana Chivvis、Sean Cole、Chana Joffe-Walt、Seth Lind、Miki Meek、Alvin Melathe、Nadia Reiman、Robyn Semien、Christopher Swetala和Matt Tierney。我们的资深制作人是Brian Reed。我们的主编是Susan Burton。今天的混音帮助来自Katherine Rae Mondo和Sharif Youssef。Sarah Koenig和Nancy Updike提供了编辑帮助。特别感谢Rebecca [? Vitale-Dokolah, ?] Nava EtShalom, [? Amina ?] [? Kotkin, ?] 和Matt Chase。

01:02:00.720 --> 01:02:29.910
<v Ira Glass>It feels crazy to say this, but this is the very last week we are working with two of the people who you never hear on the radio but who have helped run the administrative side of things here at our radio show just for years-- Elise Bergerson and Kimberly Henderson. They are both off to bigger adventures elsewhere. We are so dependent on them and on a million things they do every day. It is not entirely clear how this is going to work around here, for those of us who are still here. If we are not on the air next week, that is the reason why. You guys, we will miss you. Come back. Visit.
<v Ira Glass>说出这话感觉很疯狂，但这确实是我们与两位人员共事的最后一周，你们在广播中从未听到过，但他们只是多年来一直帮助我们运营广播节目行政方面的事——Elise Bergerson和Kimberly Henderson。她们都要去别处进行更大的冒险。我们非常依赖她们，依赖她们每天做的数百万件事。对于我们这些还在这里的人来说，这里将如何运作还不太清楚。如果下周我们没在广播中，这就是原因。你们，我们会想念你们的。回来。拜访。

01:02:29.910 --> 01:02:52.900
<v Ira Glass>Our website, thisamericanlife.org, where you can listen to our archive of over 600 episodes for absolutely free. Or get the This American Life app. This American Life is delivered to public radio stations by PRX, the Public Radio Exchange. Thanks, as always, to our program's co-founder, Mr. Torey Malatia. You know, he keeps infiltrating my Facebook account. And when I call and ask him why, why are you doing this, he says--
<v Ira Glass>我们的网站，thisamericanlife.org，在那里你可以完全免费收听我们超过600集的档案。或者获取This American Life应用程序。This American Life由PRX，公共广播交易所交付给公共广播电台。像往常一样，感谢我们节目的联合创始人Torey Malatia先生。你知道，他一直在渗透我的Facebook账户。当我打电话问他为什么，你为什么这么做，他说——

01:02:52.900 --> 01:02:54.500
<v LaDonna Powell>I'm a Russian bad boy.
<v LaDonna Powell>我是个俄罗斯坏小子。

01:02:54.500 --> 01:02:59.500
<v Ira Glass>I'm Ira Glass. Back next week with more stories of This American Life.
<v Ira Glass>我是Ira Glass。下周回来，带来更多《美国生活》的故事。
